                        "sense_id": "485b9f0c-26d9-37a9-b55e-36de3febd9cf",
                        "entry_id": "71841890-7ff4-316e-9e6c-3b6e8c45307c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "беспокоить, возбуждать страх, вызывать опасения в ком-либо за что-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "81589dd9-f35f-371c-95cc-11c58a08871a",
                        "entry_id": "71841890-7ff4-316e-9e6c-3b6e8c45307c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "пугать, вызывать страх"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a82d4353-0bfa-45be-9476-6b8520662558",
                                "sense_id": "81589dd9-f35f-371c-95cc-11c58a08871a",
                                "text": "Солёные помидоры, мочёные яблоки, квашеная капуста, жгучие перцы и маринованный чеснок, зелень, варёная рыба, жареные куры, холодец, пироги и пирожки, самодельная колбаса, сало и самогон в бутылях времён Гражданской скорее страшили, чем радовали."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e05355a0-2a32-4ce4-a8f8-0f0580c5ed4e",
                        "source_entry_id": "71841890-7ff4-316e-9e6c-3b6e8c45307c",
                        "target_lang_word": "frighten",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "frighten",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fb91ea8f-8491-3e5a-9ca9-49bc7eed5cb5",
                                        "entry_id": "c6b86c1e-9cfe-3fef-bbb3-02920a44c69f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cause to feel fear; to scare; to cause to feel alarm or fright."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c2faf77-99f3-45fa-a5c7-561589b803fa",
                                                "sense_id": "fb91ea8f-8491-3e5a-9ca9-49bc7eed5cb5",
                                                "text": "Avery puts a sheet over her head, pretending to be a ghost to frighten Emily."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e490a4f2-8737-488b-8994-68e934c579f1",
                                                "sense_id": "fb91ea8f-8491-3e5a-9ca9-49bc7eed5cb5",
                                                "text": "His Deſign was only to frighten France, and get more Money."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0be54a8-432e-430b-9af2-be99bbdfb044",
                                                "sense_id": "fb91ea8f-8491-3e5a-9ca9-49bc7eed5cb5",
                                                "text": "You may frighten a pig, a goose, a frog, and even a fly, but you cannot frighten or surprise a sloth."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f72a118c-44f4-4329-87f0-3a19702404ed",
                                                "sense_id": "fb91ea8f-8491-3e5a-9ca9-49bc7eed5cb5",
                                                "text": "And he commanded his soldiers […] to frighten them with fierce swords, but the hearts of the holy men did not quail, and they were unable to alter their words."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e286bc39-4875-3132-9ce4-f6e9fd8e2543",
                                        "entry_id": "c6b86c1e-9cfe-3fef-bbb3-02920a44c69f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To become scared or alarmed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45087b19-a40b-4d61-a29f-b2525ecd1e63",
                                                "sense_id": "e286bc39-4875-3132-9ce4-f6e9fd8e2543",
                                                "text": "In fitting the White Leghorns for exhibition, it must be remembered that they are of nervous disposition and frighten easily."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64e0243e-0d9c-46fd-b6ef-d8ab6d49e82d",
                                                "sense_id": "e286bc39-4875-3132-9ce4-f6e9fd8e2543",
                                                "text": "Those male moose at the southeast arm didn't frighten very much when we docked to fly-fish one day. One was so scared of us he just walked toward us and snorted."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c59c2863-0722-48d1-8f02-df5a5432818a",
                                                "sense_id": "e286bc39-4875-3132-9ce4-f6e9fd8e2543",
                                                "text": "Be sneaky. Fish frighten easily."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
